    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0229" n="155" xml:id="pg155"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward to Mr. Yeaman.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 14.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 18, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of the 23d instant, No. 13,
                    has been received, and that part of it relating to the articles, now in your
                    custody, which formerly belonged to the iron-clad Stoerkodder, or Stonewall, has
                    been referred to the Secretary of the Navy, who, in a letter just received at
                    this department, suggests that the articles referred to be shipped to the United
                    States for the purpose of being placed on board that vessel. You are
                    consequently instructed to lose no time in giving effect to the suggestion of
                    the Secretary of the Navy.</p>
                <p>The information communicated in your despatch concerning political affairs in
                    Denmark has been read with much interest.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">George H. Yeaman,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
